  "process_doc": "Source: TRV-001 - Approve a Travel Request. Modeling judgments: Travel Approver and Travel Request System are lanes because they own explicit main-path steps. Requestor is not modeled as a lane because the extraction gives no task or lane handoff for that actor. Option A steps are assigned to the Travel Approver lane because their text identifies that actor but contains no bold-actor metadata. The option-entry gateway follows the system display of the approval button, where the option trigger can be evaluated. Option A rejoins before the system records approval because its final step selects the approval button. The precondition that the approver received the email link is modeled as the start event.",
